id: pm-beads-v9r1
title: Track pinned merge installer drift against the committed extension fence
description: "Pre-existing infrastructure follow-up discovered while verifying PR #160. The committed .gitattributes is identical to origin/main and declares the extensions subtree with -merge. The pinned pm installer changes that entry to merge=text during npm ci. Restoring the unrelated generated change leaves isolated strict health reporting merge_fence_drift:2. The acknowledgement fix does not change this policy or dependency pins. Existing feature pm-beads-i59r already mentioned bootstrap-fence drift; searches for merge_fence_drift and bootstrap found no dedicated follow-up."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-22T12:16:36.297Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T13:09:14.362Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Choose and document the intended extension merge policy; verify install and strict health against it using the supported pinned toolchain; preserve append-only tracker history.
repro_steps: "Run npm ci and inspect the generated .gitattributes diff. Restore only that generated change, then run the pinned pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers with an empty home and no global Git configuration."
expected_result: The installer and strict health agree with the repository-owned extension merge policy without unrelated tracked changes.
actual_result: "The installer replaces -merge with merge=text; restoring the repository policy yields merge_fence_drift:2 in isolated strict health."
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T19:44:41.991Z",codex-agent,Observed the existing pinned installer fence drift during the sidecar feature work (pm-beads-je7c). The installer modifies the committed extension fence during npm ci; restored its incidental worktree change and made no installer changes. Also observed a local global-extension/host pin mismatch; clean CI validation is checked separately. Existing append-only history remains untouched.
  "2026-10-24T13:09:14.362Z",codex-agent,"PR 165 ambient-defaults review reproduced the existing local health limitation with pinned SDK 2026.10.20: npm ci rewrites the committed extensions fence from -merge to merge=text; restoring that unrelated generated edit leaves merge_fence_drift:2. Local installed pm-github 2026.10.24 also reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew against the pinned host. No history or extension configuration was changed. Fresh CI runs npm ci before health and does not carry local installed extensions; its health result is the release-gate evidence."
